(Regression test: _buffer_clear only zeroes the buffer's first byte,
not the whole allocation - a NUL-scanning number-parse would read
straight through stale bytes left over from a previous longer value.)

Create a buffer called buf.
Set byte 1 of buf to '9'.
Set byte 2 of buf to '9'.
Set byte 3 of buf to '9'.
Set byte 4 of buf to '9'.
Set byte 5 of buf to '9'.
Set byte 6 of buf to '9'.
Set n1 to buf as a number.
Print n1.

clear buf.
Set byte 1 of buf to '5'.
Set n2 to buf as a number.
Print n2.

clear buf.
Set byte 1 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 2 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 3 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 4 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 5 of buf to 'f'.
Set byte 6 of buf to 'f'.
Set n3 to buf as a hex number.
Print n3.

clear buf.
Set byte 1 of buf to 'a'.
Set byte 2 of buf to 'b'.
Set n4 to buf as a hex number.
Print n4.
